ApplicationAwsSessionExpiry.description:
AWS session-expiry semantics owned by the access-profile application
configuration. Strict expiry is only valid for SAML-bound applications;
other bindings intentionally retain new-sessions-only behavior.

scope_type.description:
Optional scope for the assignment. Omission creates an unscoped
tenant-wide assignment. Every non-tenant scope requires `scope_id`;
a resource scope must also include its resource type.

BillingPaymentMethodActionResult.description:
Result of a provider-safe payment-method action.

The response contains the resulting masked method and its new revision;
it does not echo provider request diagnostics or the provider customer.

billing_period.description:
Authoritative billing window for one-time/prepaid settlement. The
provider event must echo this window before a rated charge is written;
omitting it keeps the checkout unrated rather than inventing a period.

GroupMemberSummary.description:
Customer-safe group member projection. Preview fixtures do not have a
durable assignment ledger, so their assignment coordinates are omitted;
production group members always carry them.
